# Copy this file to `.env` in this same folder if you want to override defaults.
# None of these are required to run or build the existing Camartes Customer app.

# Optional. Enables Google Places address autocomplete on the location screen.
# Leave empty to use the built-in Indian cities fallback (the booking flow still works).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=

# Public Google OAuth client IDs for Continue with Google (never put a client secret here).
# Create OAuth 2.0 clients in Google Cloud Console:
#   Web application — required for Expo web. Authorized JavaScript origins / redirect URIs
#   must include this app's web origin (for local: http://localhost:<port> and http://127.0.0.1:<port>).
#   Android — package name com.camartes.customer plus the app signing SHA-1.
#   iOS — bundle identifier com.camartes.customer.
# Camartes POST /api/auth/google verifies the Google ID token. The backend must accept
# tokens whose audience is one of these client IDs.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=

# Temporary development authentication. Source of truth is AUTH_MODE in
# src/config/authMode.ts (currently DEMO). Override here without rewriting Login:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_AUTH_MODE=DEMO  — local demo accounts, no Camartes auth calls
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_AUTH_MODE=REAL  — existing Camartes backend
# Production/release builds always force REAL and ignore DEMO.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_AUTH_MODE=

# The Camartes Vendor Platform URL is already set in source
# (https://camartes-backend.onrender.com). Do not replace it with a mock API.
